{
  "reasoning": "The current `threshold_ratio` docs and tuning table invert the monotonic behavior relative to the implemented condition `energy < local_avg × threshold_ratio`. This can cause users to tune in the wrong direction (over-removal vs missed pauses). Update the parameter description, fix the tuning table, and add practical lecture-video guidance with suggested starting point/range and cautions for low-volume/variable loudness.",
  "edits": [
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "target": "- `--threshold-ratio`: Ratio of local average for low energy (default: 0.5)",
      "content": "- `--threshold-ratio`: Low-energy cutoff as a fraction of the **local average** (default: 0.5). A second is marked “pause/low energy” when `energy < local_avg × threshold_ratio`. **Higher values** mark more seconds as pauses (more aggressive removal). **Lower values** are stricter and mark fewer pauses."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "target": "| `threshold_ratio` | More aggressive | More conservative |",
      "content": "| `threshold_ratio` | Stricter (fewer pauses detected) | More aggressive (more pauses detected) |"
    },
    {
      "op": "insert_after",
      "target": "## Parameters Tuning",
      "content": "\n\n### Practical guidance (lecture videos)\n\n- Start with `--threshold-ratio 0.5`.\n- Typical useful range: **~0.35–0.7**.\n  - If you are **missing** obvious pauses/board-writing silences, **increase** the ratio (e.g., 0.55 → 0.65).\n  - If you are **removing quiet teaching** (soft voice, mic far away), **decrease** the ratio (e.g., 0.5 → 0.4).\n- Caution: when speaker loudness changes a lot, the local average will track the change; prefer small ratio adjustments and consider increasing `--window-size` for smoother context if you see oscillation."
    }
  ]
}

